      "content": "it's hard to see a way forward when the numbers literally don't add up. like, no matter how many hours i pull, i'm always behind. it's not even about being 'sad' anymore, it's just this heavy realization that i'm basically just a servant to my own survival. it feels so pointless to keep fighting a losing battle against a system that's designed to drain you dry. it feels like i'm just waiting for the inevitable crash.",
